course: dictionary
lesson: 3344
title: Exactly: just right
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Exactly is a small word that makes a big difference. It means just right, with nothing more and nothing less. «The potoo sits still on a branch looking exactly like a dead stump.» The bird is not a bit like a stump. It is a perfect copy, so exactly means in every way.
explain: Read the words around exactly to find its meaning. «Watch the sneaky pair tu es and il est: they sound exactly the same, "ay".» The clue is the same: the two words sound identical, not nearly identical. «A robot follows its steps exactly» means it does each step with no mistakes. Try swapping in just right: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the meaning.
explain: Exactly can also be a one-word answer. If someone says, «Exactly!», they mean yes, that is completely right. Listen for the tone and the words before it, and you will know which meaning is needed.
fact: Exactly means just right, not more and not less.
fact: Exactly can mean in every way, as in «exactly the same».
fact: «Exactly!» means yes, that is completely right.
fact: «Exactly which» in «which is exactly why the tricks are used» means precisely the reason.
fact: A quick check is to swap in just right or precisely; if the sentence still works, exactly is being used correctly.
exercise: «The potoo sits still on a branch looking exactly like a dead stump.» What does exactly mean here? | Far away from the branch | Only a little | *Just like, in every way | Very quickly
exercise: «Watch the sneaky pair tu es and il est: they sound exactly the same.» What does exactly the same mean? | Louder than before | Not the same at all | Almost the same, but a bit different | *Completely the same, in every way
exercise: Ella says «Exactly!» when Sam answers the question. What does she mean? | Please be quiet now | No, that is wrong | Let us go home | *Yes, that is completely right
test: «The robot follows its steps exactly.» What does exactly suggest? | *Doing every step with no mistakes | Following the steps when it feels like it | Running away from the steps | Skipping the steps to go faster
test: The bus came exactly on time. What does exactly on time mean? | A little early, but nobody minded | Very late, after lunch | *Precisely on time, not early or late | Sometime during the morning
exam: «The stonefish looks exactly like a lumpy stone.» What does exactly mean here? | Quite a lot | *Just like, in every way | Once in a while | Badly
